# XSH gmtime(), gmtime_r()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Every time value used is non-negative and in a year from 1970 on, where
# XBD 4.19 defines the relationship. Values past 2038 are used only where
# time_t can hold them (XBD <sys/types.h> asks for 64 bits since 2024).

assertion  XSH.gmtime.001
anchor     functions/gmtime.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.19
class      required
since      1988
says       For a set of times from the Epoch to the year 2400 (leap days,
           the ends of leap and common years, 2100 as a common century
           year, 2000 and 2400 as leap ones, and the start of every
           month of 1999 to 2001), gmtime() returns a structure whose
           tm_sec, tm_min, tm_hour, tm_yday and tm_year give the value
           through the XBD 4.19 expression, whose tm_mon and tm_mday name
           the same day of the Gregorian calendar as tm_yday, whose
           tm_wday counts from Thursday 1 January 1970, all within their
           <time.h> ranges, and whose tm_isdst is 0.
note       TZ names a zone 3 hours west of UTC during the test, so a
           conversion to local time is seen. tm_isdst is 0 because a UTC
           time has no Daylight Saving Time (<time.h>: 0 when DST is not
           in effect).
test       t/001-utc-fields.c

assertion  XSH.gmtime.002
anchor     functions/gmtime.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       gmtime_r() stores into *result the same broken-down time as
           XSH.gmtime.001 describes, for the same set of times, and
           returns result.
test       t/002-gmtime-r.c

assertion  XSH.gmtime.003
anchor     functions/gmtime.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/time.h.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       After gmtime_r(), tm_zone points to the string "UTC" and
           tm_gmtoff is 0; the string still reads "UTC" after TZ is
           changed and tzset(), localtime() and gmtime_r() are called
           again.
note       Names tm_gmtoff and tm_zone; a system whose <time.h> hides
           them under the strict build cannot compile the test.
test       t/003-gmtime-r-zone.c

assertion  XSH.gmtime.005
anchor     functions/gmtime.html#ERRORS/EOVERFLOW
anchor     functions/gmtime.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       gmtime() of the largest time_t value, whose year cannot be
           held in tm_year, returns a null pointer and sets errno to
           EOVERFLOW.
note       UNRESOLVED where int is wide enough to hold that year.
test       t/005-eoverflow.c

assertion  XSH.gmtime.006
anchor     functions/gmtime.html#ERRORS/EOVERFLOW
anchor     functions/gmtime.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       gmtime_r() of the largest time_t value returns a null pointer
           and sets errno to EOVERFLOW.
note       UNRESOLVED where int is wide enough to hold that year.
test       t/006-r-eoverflow.c
